[205.666469, "o", "aye noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n317:\r\n318:Interview #340 with fixed assets highlighted how capital project capitalization statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n319:\r\n320:## Case Study 03 — Sox Sampling Mismatch\r\n321:\r\n322:Interview #796 with internal audit highlighted how SOX sampling mismatch statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n323:\r\n324:Follow-up #231 confirmed that internal audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for SOX sampling mismatch. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n325:"]
[205.666485, "o", "\r\n326:Interview #737 with internal audit highlighted how SOX sampling mismatch statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n327:\r\n328:Risk assessment WP-5795 ties SOX sampling mismatch to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n329:\r\n330:Interview #266 with internal audit highlighted how SOX sampling mismatch statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n331:\r\n332:Follow-up #130 confirmed that internal audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for SOX sampling mismatch. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n333:\r\n334:Follow-up #559 confirmed that internal audit had been using an inform"]
