[206.732545, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r13:252:## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n14-253:\r\n15-254:Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n16-255:\r\n17-256:Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n18-257:amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n19-258:output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n20-259:rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n21-260:contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n22-261:\r\n23:262:## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence — field notes\r\n24-263:\r\n25-264:Risk assessment WP-2138 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n26-265:\r\n27-266:Working paper WP-3210 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor "]
[206.732607, "o", "runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n28-267:\r\n29-268:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n30-269:\r\n31-270:Working paper WP-6073 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n32-271:\r\n33-272:Lead reviewer J. Huang noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n34-273:\r\n35-274:The committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owne"]
[206.73262, "o", "r change.\r\n36-275:\r\n37-276:Lead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n38-277:\r\n39-278:Follow-up #238 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n40-279:\r\n41-280:Working paper WP-3893 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n42-281:\r\n43-282:In July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n44-283:\r\n45-284:"]
[206.732631, "o", "Memo WP-2881 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n46-285:\r\n47-286:During July review, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n48-287:\r\n49-288:Interview #586 with fixed assets highlighted how capital project capitalization statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n50-289:\r\n51-290:Risk assessment WP-4038 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n52-291:\r\n53-292:Working paper WP-2952 documents a three-way match"]
[206.732642, "o", " failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n54-293:\r\n55-294:The committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n56-295:\r\n57-296:In July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n58-297:\r\n59-298:Site visit #156 to fixed assets captured mailbox exports showing how capital project capitalization correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n60-299:\r\n61-300:During July review, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Fin"]
[206.732656, "o", "ance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n62-301:\r\n63-302:In July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@64435c900e2e:/app# "]
