[207.806272, "o", "19:468:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n20-469:\r\n21-470:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n22-471:\r\n23-472:The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n24-473:messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n25-474:`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n26-475:equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n27-476:apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n28-477:after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n29-478:\r\n30:479:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing — field notes\r\n31-480:\r\n32-481:Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n33-482:\r\n34-483:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-bin"]
[207.806322, "o", "ding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n35-484:\r\n36-485:Memo WP-3037 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n37-486:\r\n38-487:In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n39-488:\r\n40-489:Working paper WP-7415 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n41-490:\r\n42-491:The committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing facto"]
[207.806332, "o", "r to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n43-492:\r\n44-493:Site visit #268 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n45-494:\r\n46-495:In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n47-496:\r\n48-497:In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n49-498:\r\n50-499:Risk assessment WP-3524 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around ma"]
