[208.684496, "o", "16:685:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n17-686:\r\n18-687:Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n19-688:\r\n20-689:The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n21-690:target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n22-691:greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n23-692:`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n24-693:applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n25-694:both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n26-695:\r\n27:696:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence — field notes\r\n28-697:\r\n29-698:Site visit #195 to corporate accounting captured mailbox exports showing how intercompany netting dispute correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n30-699:\r\n31-700:Duri"]
