[212.012987, "o", "22:1201:## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n23-1202:\r\n24-1203:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n25-1204:\r\n26-1205:Exception coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n27-1206:`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n28-1207:when final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n29-1208:that transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n30-1209:comparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n31-1210:(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n32-1211:lexical order of the reason codes.\r\n33-1212:\r\n34:1213:## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I) — field notes\r\n35-1214:\r\n36-1215:Memo WP-7758 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n37-1216:\r"]
