[370.54366, "o", "468:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n469-\r\n470-Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n471-\r\n472-The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n473-messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n474-`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n475-equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n476-apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n477-after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n478-\r\n479:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing — field notes\r\n480-\r\n481-Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n482-\r\n483-Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mai"]
[370.543756, "o", "l against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n484-\r\n485-Memo WP-3037 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n486-\r\n487-In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n488-\r\n489-Working paper WP-7415 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n490-\r\n491-The committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts ag"]
[370.543802, "o", "ainst amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n492-\r\n493-Site visit #268 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n494-\r\n495-In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n496-\r\n497-In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n498-\r\n499-Risk assessment WP-3524 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative"]
[370.543819, "o", " transaction sources.\r\n500-\r\n501-Memo WP-3030 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n502-\r\n503-Working paper WP-4438 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n504-\r\n505-Memo WP-1550 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n506-\r\n507-During December freeze, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n508-\r\n509-In December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end "]
