[371.781642, "o", "685:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n686-\r\n687-Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n688-\r\n689-The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n690-target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n691-greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n692-`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n693-applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n694-both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n695-\r\n696:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence — field notes\r\n697-\r\n698-Site visit #195 to corporate accounting captured mailbox exports showing how intercompany netting dispute correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n699-\r\n700-During April settlement, R. Okonkwo circulated a dra"]
