[373.506437, "o", "1058:## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n1059-\r\n1060-Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n1061-\r\n1062-Auditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n1063-ledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n1064-sets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n1065-`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n1066-keep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\n1067-places in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n1068-\r\n1069:## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output — field notes\r\n1070-\r\n1071-Follow-up #977 confirmed that external audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for revenue cutoff testing. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n1072-\r\n1073-Memo WP-3912 summarizes stakeholder interviews about revenue cutoff testing. Participants disagreed on whethe"]
[373.508602, "o", "r unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n1074-\r\n1075-Follow-up #283 confirmed that external audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for revenue cutoff testing. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n1076-\r\n1077-Memo WP-9083 summarizes stakeholder interviews about revenue cutoff testing. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n1078-\r\n1079-Interview #648 with external audit highlighted how revenue cutoff testing statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n1080-\r\n1081-Follow-up #929 confirmed that external audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for revenue cutoff testing. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonic"]
[373.508986, "o", "al ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n1082-\r\n1083-The committee packet references revenue cutoff testing as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n1084-\r\n1085-During September fieldwork, J. Huang circulated a draft finding on revenue cutoff testing. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n1086-\r\n1087-Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that revenue cutoff testing created reconciliation noise in external audit during September fieldwork. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n1088-\r\n1089-Risk assessment WP-2640 ties revenue cutoff testing to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n1090-\r\n1091-Working paper WP-7221 documents a "]
