[374.720648, "o", "1201:## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n1202-\r\n1203-Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n1204-\r\n1205-Exception coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n1206-`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n1207-when final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n1208-that transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n1209-comparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n1210-(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n1211-lexical order of the reason codes.\r\n1212-\r\n1213:## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I) — field notes\r\n1214-\r\n1215-Memo WP-7758 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n1216-\r\n1217-In Q1 close, external advisors reviewed ve"]
[374.720892, "o", "ndor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n1218-\r\n1219-During Q1 close, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n1220-\r\n1221-Risk assessment WP-8021 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n1222-\r\n1223-Working paper WP-3669 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n1224-\r\n1225-Site visit #351 to procurement captured mailbox exports showing how vendor onboarding backlog correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Rev"]
[374.720912, "o", "iewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n1226-\r\n1227-Memo WP-1992 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n1228-\r\n1229-The committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n1230-\r\n1231-Lead reviewer J. Huang noted that vendor onboarding backlog created reconciliation noise in procurement during Q1 close. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n1232-\r\n1233-Follow-up #132 confirmed that procurement had been using an informal spreadsheet for vendor onboarding backlog. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end."]
